WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:08.703
A transition bus feeds a fast notifier and an audit writer that needs one second per row.

2
00:00:08.703 --> 00:00:11.387
It has two spare slots, and DROP_LATEST.

3
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:14.775
Six transitions arrive, 10 milliseconds apart.

4
00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:17.029
What does the fast notifier get?

5
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:24.763
Picture one tape that every subscriber reads, each with its own playback head.

6
00:00:24.763 --> 00:00:26.835
There is no queue per subscriber.

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.277
The audit writer takes 1 and is busy for a second.

8
00:00:30.277 --> 00:00:32.046
2 and 3 fill the two slots.

9
00:00:32.046 --> 00:00:36.044
The notifier reads them, but the audit head still needs them.

10
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.792
So 4 finds the tape full, and DROP_LATEST drops it for everyone, then 5 and 6.

11
00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:45.664
The slowest subscriber decided what the fast one gets.

12
00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:48.035
A StateFlow has no tape.

13
00:00:48.035 --> 00:00:50.225
It is a notice board with one slot.

14
00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:55.044
Pinning a sheet equal to the one on the board does nothing, and wakes nobody.

15
00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.775
A reader busy for 100 milliseconds per value misses the board going to CAPTURED and back to AUTHORIZED.

16
00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:06.691
When it looks up, the sheet matches the last one it read, so it sees nothing.

17
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.453
stateIn and shareIn launch one coroutine: a pump, with a tap for each subscriber.

18
00:01:13.453 --> 00:01:17.427
WhileSubscribed(5_000) puts the tap on a motion sensor.

19
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.169
Dashboard A arrives at 0 and the pump starts: 100, 101, 102.

20
00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:28.088
A leaves at 2.5 seconds, and a 5 second timer starts.

21
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:29.911
A is back at 4 seconds.

22
00:01:29.911 --> 00:01:35.704
The timer is cancelled, the pump never stopped, and A gets 104 from the same run.

23
00:01:35.867 --> 00:01:37.370
A leaves at 6 seconds.

24
00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:41.128
This time the timer runs out, and the pump stops at 11.

25
00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.171
At 14 seconds A returns.

26
00:01:43.171 --> 00:01:45.392
It gets the stale 111 first.

27
00:01:45.392 --> 00:01:49.756
Then the upstream restarts from the top, and sends 200.

28
00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:56.560
Set replayExpirationMillis to 0, and the stale value is thrown out when the pump stops.

29
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.405
Reactor's twin is replay(1) with refCount.

30
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.336
So one source feeds many readers.

31
00:02:02.336 --> 00:02:11.008
The slowest fills a SharedFlow's tape, a StateFlow keeps the latest, and WhileSubscribed pumps while someone is there, plus 5 seconds.

32
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.059
Quick check.

33
00:02:12.059 --> 00:02:14.853
A leaves at 6 seconds and is back at 9.

34
00:02:14.853 --> 00:02:17.001
Does the upstream start again?
